# Create Project

Create a product project next to this framework. Do not invent an `Approved` stack.

## When to use

Use this from the factory framework repository (`sw-ai-factory`), or from any checkout that has the `factory` CLI. After the project exists, open that directory and follow its `AGENTS.md`.

## Inputs

Collect only what the owner already stated:

- Project folder name.
- Optional `--intake FILE.yaml` (a `ProjectIntake` document).
- Optional `--from-specs FILE.md` (owner-written `project-specs.md`).
- Optional `--preset web-app|api|cli|mobile` to fill blank stack and command fields as `Proposed`.
- Optional `--tool` values from `codex`, `cursor`, `claude-code`, `grok`. Default is every supported tool.
- `--copy` when a Git submodule is not wanted.

If more than three open questions remain, write a clarification artifact instead of blocking on chat.

## Command

```bash
factory init <project-name> --no-interactive \
  [--intake FILE.yaml] [--from-specs FILE.md] [--preset PRESET] \
  [--tool TOOL] [--copy] [--tool-kit instructions]
```

Skills emit by default. Pass `--no-skills` only when the owner asks.

Do not run the Textual wizard. Do not mark technology `Approved`. Do not scaffold source in this skill.

## After init

1. Report the created path and `Factory link`.
2. Tell the owner to open that project.
3. Next skills there: complete `TASK-0001`, then `onboard-specs` or `create-requirement`, then `factory ready` before implementation.
